-- NOTE: compose / flip RETURN a function. The loader's signatureFromSig
-- flattens the whole arrow spine into params, so a faithful `(a -> c)`
-- return would make compose arity-3 / flip arity-2 and the evaluator's
-- arity gate (json-logic.ts:1550) would yield a partial instead of the
-- composed closure. To preserve the runtime-correct arity (2 / 1) their
-- return is an opaque var `r`; the precise function-return type is a
-- sig-surface gap deferred to FM-retire-10 (like the 4 type-returners).
module std where

@native
@label "Named SetExpr"
@description "Reference a registered named set (NAMED_SETS) by name as a SetExpr value `{$ref: name}`. Irreducible host bridge — Fenel record literals can't author a `$`-prefixed key. String → SetExpr."
@tags "set" "named" "substrate-leaf"
